# SynapseDesk — third-party code

## web_ar_canvas/public/rig-geometry.mjs

Vendored verbatim from `rig/rigtest2/js/rig/geometry.js` in this repository, which carries
`SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later`. It is the Pepper's-ghost projection maths: plane
reflection plus Kooima's generalized off-axis perspective through the monitor's mirror image.
It was written dependency-free (plain arrays in, plain arrays out) specifically so it could be
reused like this, and it is kept byte-identical so fixes flow in either direction.

**This has a licensing consequence and it has not been decided.** Combining GPL-3.0-or-later
code with the rest of SynapseDesk means the combined work must be distributed under
GPL-3.0-or-later. SynapseDesk currently declares no licence at all — neither a LICENSE file nor
a `license` field in `pyproject.toml`. Before this is published or shipped to anyone, either:

  - adopt GPL-3.0-or-later for SynapseDesk (add the licence text and set it in pyproject), or
  - drop this file and reach the rig over HTTP instead of linking its code, keeping the two
    works separate.

Nothing here decides that. It is recorded so the choice is made deliberately.
